-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- HAND-PORTED: seed the initial Configuration for the built-in storage providers.
--
-- The transpiler dropped all seven UPDATEs. Nothing else in this release carries them: they are
-- not mj-sync-managed rows, so `mj sync push` does not re-seed them, and `mj codegen` regenerates
-- routines rather than data. Left out, the column would exist on PostgreSQL and stay NULL for
-- every provider -- and the whole point of the column is to move UI branding (IconClass,
-- BrandColor) out of hardcoded client mappings and into metadata, so a NULL bag means Explorer
-- has neither an icon nor a brand colour for any storage provider on PostgreSQL.
--
-- The Configuration column is TEXT here (the T-SQL side is NVARCHAR(MAX)), so the JSON is written
